---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Em from "../components/Em.astro";
import SectionMarker from "../components/SectionMarker.astro";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Codepawl is a solo dev tools studio for engineers shipping AI systems. The pawl-and-ratchet metaphor explains how we ship."
>
  {/* Hero */}
  <section class="border-b border-ink-700/60">
    <div class="page-section mx-auto max-w-container py-24 lg:py-32">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-technical text-ratchet-500">
        About Codepawl
      </p>
      <h1
        class="display-headline mt-10 text-4xl text-ink-50 md:text-7xl"
        style="line-height: 1.05;"
      >
        Solo studio, <Em>unreasonable</Em> depth.
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Body */}
  <section class="border-b border-ink-700/60">
    <div class="page-section mx-auto max-w-container py-24 lg:py-section">
      <SectionMarker number="001" label="Who runs it" />
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12">
        <div class="space-y-6 lg:col-span-8 lg:col-start-1">
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-200">
            Codepawl is a one-person dev tools studio. I run product, design,
            engineering, support, and the build log. Currently based in Ho Chi
            Minh City, planning a move to Berlin in the next twelve to eighteen
            months.
          </p>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-200">
            Funding floor comes from freelance challenge work for AI companies.
            That pays for time spent on Codepawl. No VC, no advisors, no growth
            target other than shipping the next product on the list.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-b border-ink-700/60">
    <div class="page-section mx-auto max-w-container py-24 lg:py-section">
      <SectionMarker number="002" label="The metaphor" />
      <h2 class="display-headline mt-10 max-w-3xl text-3xl text-ink-50 md:text-5xl">
        A pawl locks a <Em>ratchet</Em> wheel one tooth at a time.
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12">
        <div class="space-y-6 lg:col-span-8 lg:col-start-1">
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-200">
            The pawl is the small arm. The ratchet is the toothed wheel. Together
            they let motion go forward and prevent it from slipping back. That's
            our model for shipping. Each release locks in. Each product locks in
            on the previous one.
          </p>
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-200">
            This is how we ratchet engineering forward: small, irreversible
            commits to the codebase, the brand, and the product line. Boring
            mechanism, compounding result.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-b border-ink-700/60">
    <div class="page-section mx-auto max-w-container py-24 lg:py-section">
      <SectionMarker number="003" label="What we ship" />
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12">
        <div class="space-y-6 lg:col-span-8 lg:col-start-1">
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-200">
            The first product is <a
              href="/diagnose"
              class="text-ratchet-300 transition-colors hover:text-ratchet-500"
              >Codepawl Trace</a
            >, a failure-explanation layer for AI agent developers. Read your
            existing traces, return a structured diagnosis. Future products will
            target other bottlenecks in the AI build loop.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="page-section mx-auto max-w-container py-24 lg:py-section">
      <SectionMarker number="004" label="Philosophy" />
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12">
        <div class="space-y-6 lg:col-span-8 lg:col-start-1">
          <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-200">
            Open source where reasonable. Self-host as a real option, not a
            checkbox. Pricing that a hobbyist can afford and a team can justify.
            No growth-hacker tactics, no fake social proof, no waitlist
            choreography. Just shipped products and the build log next to them.
          </p>
        </div>
        <aside class="border-t border-ink-700/60 pt-8 lg:col-span-4 lg:border-l lg:border-t-0 lg:pl-8 lg:pt-0">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-technical text-ratchet-500">
            Connect
          </p>
          <div class="mt-6 space-y-7">
            <div>
              <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-technical text-ink-500">
                Builder
              </p>
              <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 font-mono text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-200">
                <li>
                  <a
                    href="https://github.com/lunovian"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="transition-colors hover:text-ratchet-300"
                  >
                    GitHub · @lunovian
                  </a>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <a
                    href="https://x.com/lunovian"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="transition-colors hover:text-ratchet-300"
                  >
                    X · @lunovian
                  </a>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-technical text-ink-500">
                Product
              </p>
              <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 font-mono text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-200">
                <li>
                  <a
                    href="https://github.com/codepawl"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="transition-colors hover:text-ratchet-300"
                  >
                    GitHub · @codepawl
                  </a>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <a
                    href="https://x.com/codepawl"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                    class="transition-colors hover:text-ratchet-300"
                  >
                    X · @codepawl
                  </a>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
